# Aamaan Sharrma's portfolio

A conversational portfolio inspired by the supplied Framer reference, built with React 18, Vite, React Router and GSAP. Includes five résumé-based case studies, experience, skills, education, freelance services, contact links and a local portfolio guide.

## Run locally

```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open the URL Vite prints, with `/Portfolio/` appended. For the production version:

```sh
npm run build
npm run serve:production
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:4400/Portfolio/`.

## Edit content

- `src/data/site.js`: biography metadata, projects, experience, skills and services. The supplied résumé is the source of truth; it supersedes older content still retained in the repository.
- `src/Portfolio.jsx`: active interface, routes and the curated question matcher.
- `src/portfolio.css`: responsive layout and visual tokens.
- `public/Aamaan-Sharrma.pdf`: downloadable résumé.
- `DESIGN.md`: design rationale and content assumptions.

The guide answers a small set of topics locally. It does not call an LLM, send messages, store chat history or require an API key. Unsupported questions receive an explicit fallback. Email buttons open the visitor's email app.

## Build and publish

The build prerenders 14 routes, an HTML 404 page and a sitemap. It retains the existing `/Portfolio/` GitHub Pages base. The URL in `src/data/site.js`, `index.html` and `public/robots.txt` comes from the résumé. Update these and `vite.config.js` if changing hosts.

`npm run deploy` publishes `dist` through the existing gh-pages configuration. Only run it when ready to publish. This implementation has not been deployed.

Before publishing, review current freelance availability and employer-work descriptions. No portrait was provided, so the interface uses an AS monogram. No testimonials, client logos, prices or additional project results were invented.

## Verification

With the production server running, `node scripts/verify.mjs .shots/review` checks each route at desktop, mobile and reduced-motion settings; runs axe; verifies menu focus, project filters, guide answers and résumé availability. It uses the installed awwwards skill's browser launcher from `~/.codex/skills/awwwards/scripts/browser.mjs`, plus project-local Playwright and axe-core. Screenshots and reports are ignored by Git.
## System
Ground #ffffff; sidebar #f7f7f8; ink #202123; muted #62666b; line #e7e7e9; accent #176b50.
System sans-serif (Segoe UI / Arial) intentionally follows the familiar application interface, needs no font downloads and has no font layout shift. Headings 28–38px; body 16px / 1.65; UI 13–14px. Main reading measure 760px. Sidebar 260px. Gutter 24px mobile / 48px desktop. Radius 10px UI / 24px composer.
Home: [sidebar] [top tabs / availability] [centered monogram + greeting / composer / suggested topic grid] [footer].
Projects: [sidebar] [heading / category tabs / numbered rows with summaries] [composer].
Case: [sidebar] [question bubble / author / title / result / narrative / media / next project] [composer].
Contact: [sidebar] [question / contact invitation / services / email action] [composer].
Mobile: top menu button, modal drawer, single reading column, wrapped bubbles, composer in document flow. No nested scrolling for project lists.

## Decisions and assumptions
- Preserve the user's requested reference rather than forcing a different award-site concept. No WebGL, loader or decorative idle movement. Native scrolling is appropriate to this application-like reading experience; Lenis is installed but deliberately not activated.
- GSAP handles route entry via a scoped cleanup hook. Reduced-motion preferences disable motion. Native pointer and keyboard focus remain visible.
- The composer is a local curated portfolio guide, explicitly labeled. No live LLM, network request or invented AI response; unknown questions receive a helpful fallback and contact link. No chat history stored.
- Short display name is Aamaan Sharrma; full résumé name is Aamaan Ssanjay Sharrma. New résumé dates and metrics replace older repository claims.
- Service descriptions are inferred from demonstrated skills and the user's stated freelance intent. No price, availability hours, client testimonials or turnaround promises invented.
- No portrait provided: use AS monogram. Project visuals are existing repository assets where relevant. Employer projects use text case studies and employer attribution, not invented screenshots.
- GitHub Pages URL is taken from the résumé. Static route output will support direct navigation on that host. Publishing is separate from local implementation.

## Release review
Owner should confirm employer project descriptions are suitable for public sharing, current availability and the résumé contact details before publishing. This is a local implementation, not a deployment.
